      "side": 1,
      "message": "rr11 is not one I\u0027d expect. `a000` vs. `a001` is a bit of a toss-up but one of them arises regularly with red/alpha handling. The same goes for `rrr1` vs. `rrra` for red/gray handling.  The rgb/bgr comes up in data swizzles but less so for shading swizzles since that re-ordering is handled by the GPU.  `argb` and `abgr` are also valid format channel orders but I don\u0027t think I\u0027d ever really see their inverse.  But I wanted to cover more involved cases and try to find ones where the inverse wasn\u0027t just identical to itself.",
